The  driver  provides  support  for  the Aztech/PackardBell radio
cards.  The Aztech/PackardBell cards are stereo  FM  tuners  that
allow  tuning  in  the 87.5‐108.0 MHz range.  They are capable of
reporting signal status (tuned/not tuned, stereo/mono signal) and
forcing audio output to mono.  The Aztech cards use only one  I/O
port.   The  I/O port is set by the driver to the value specified
in the configuration file.  The I/O port must be one of 0x350 and
0x358.  The device driver appeared in and The driver was  written
by  and The man page was written by It is impossible to determine
to which frequency the card is tuned.  Thus, the driver will  re‐
port  an  internally  stored  value  even  if  it  is not correct
(changed by some program that uses direct port access).
